### Critical Realism Assessment (Challenges & Mitigations)
- **Gas & Computation**: Verification feasible at 1.5–2.5 M (optimizable via n-phase proofs and Cairo batching). Full on-chain generation impossible (sequential by design) — sidecar is the only realistic path.  
- **Hardware Centralization**: ASICs exist but Chia’s distribution model + rate-limiting prevent monopoly (proven in 5+ years live operation).  
- **Security**: Sequentiality resists grinding; class-group unknown order + Wesolowski proven sound. Post-quantum lattice variants available for long-term upgrade.  
- **Cairo Feasibility**: No native class-group support yet, but modular ops + Poseidon suffice (precedent in Starknet ZKML and heavy-circuit projects). 2026 Cairo 2.x improvements close the gap.  
- **2028 Timeline**: Testnet mock in 2026 → full Wesolowski verifier + Chia sidecar pilots in 2027 → production BitDMX in 2028. Matches Starknet grant realism (no vaporware).

